# Phone account

A Belarus mobile confirmed by SMS is a real account. It does not wait for a mailbox. The stored login stays `pending.{id}@users.trenio.invalid` so a letter is never sent there. Screens do not show that address.

## What a person sees

- No chosen name yet: the given name is the mask `+37529.....51` (`maskedBelarusPhone`). The operator code stays, five digits become dots, the last two stay.
- Where the pending mailbox would be shown (account row, review author, trainer account mail): the compact number `+375298516745` (`compactBelarusPhone` through `displayAccountLogin`). No spaces.
- A name the person typed stays. Google or Yandex may still replace the mask, the same way they replace «Пользователь».
- A real mailbox with no chosen name is signed with the part before `@` (`storedGivenName`). `dasafilon@mail.ru` is `dasafilon` on reviews and everywhere else. A pending or deleted shell does not use that part. A trainer card is not renamed to it.
- A trainer or club card is not renamed to the mask. Only a plain `user` with no trainer card takes it.
- The journal does not gain the full number. Keep storing a real mailbox, or nothing, in `subject`.

## Notices

A phone login has no mailbox. Do not send a letter to the pending address.

Only an account-safety event becomes one short SMS (`PHONE_SMS` in `src/lib/mail/notice-rules.ts`), and only when that account has no confirmed mailbox:

- the password, the mailbox, or the mobile changed
- Telegram was linked or unlinked
- a sign-in from another browser
- the account was closed

Each text fits one Cyrillic SMS (70 characters), starts with `Trenio.by:`, and carries no message body and no link.

A new direct message, a published or rejected review, and a review reply do not get an SMS. A confirmed mailbox still gets those as letters. A phone-only account stays quiet for them until this pause is lifted.

## Do

```ts
firstName: phoneSignatureName(current, phone) ?? current;
firstName: storedGivenName(typedName, email);
caption: displayAccountLogin(email, phone);
await sendQuickSms(phone, PHONE_SMS.password);
```

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: the pending mailbox is the label
<span>{user.email}</span>

// wrong: a confirmed phone is still the placeholder
firstName: "Пользователь";

// wrong: a chat or a review pings the mobile
await sendQuickSms(phone, "Trenio.by: вам написали");
```
